# Iterating on a task

- When the task or checkout changes, confirm the branch, PR/base, dirty work,
  and authorized finish step. Carry authorization within that scope, not across
  unrelated tasks. Preserve work already present.
- Inspect existing scripts, flows, and fixtures before improvising setup. For
  UI work, establish access to the consuming screen before substantial edits;
  identify missing prerequisites early.
- Reuse passing checks until relevant source, dependencies, configuration, or
  an unresolved concern changes. Serialize commands that regenerate shared
  outputs; run independent checks after those outputs are stable.
- Before handing off checkout changes, inspect flag-off/unresolved behavior,
  error completion, subscription breadth, and existing design tokens.
- Extract components by coherent responsibility and a small interface. Respect
  repository size limits, but moving all state into one large hook alone does
  not establish simpler code.
- For operational questions, lead with one recommended command. Verify the
  effective local configuration before claiming which environment it runs.
